{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>These are the generations of Noah.</b> Everywhere 'these' (אלה) is said, it invalidates the preceding ones. The preceding ones — every inclination of the thoughts of their heart was only evil all day, and they went to destruction; but Noah was a righteous man, wholehearted, and he established generations for the world." "<b>Generations of Noah.</b> In the sense of happenings and events, as in 'for you do not know what a day will give birth to' (מה ילד יום). And so Rashi explained regarding 'these are the generations of Jacob — Joseph' etc., meaning, these are the happenings and events of Noah, as it goes on to explain: that he was righteous and his generation wicked, and through their sin they were destroyed, while he escaped." "<b>A righteous man, wholehearted he was.</b> It gives the reason why he found favor more than all the people of his generation." "<b>Wholehearted (תמים).</b> Innocent. He said: everyone about whom 'wholehearted' is stated completed the years corresponding to his numerical value (תמים = 490), and Noah likewise — from that time when 'wholehearted' was stated about him, he completed and lived afterward shemittot and yovelot, for the year of the flood was not counted in the reckoning, since the orders of creation were changed in it." "<b>He was (היה).</b> Everyone about whom <b>'he was'</b> (היה) is stated saw a new world. 'Noah, a righteous man, wholehearted, <b>he was</b>' — yesterday 'and he wiped out all existence'; now 'and the sons of Noah who came out of the ark' etc. 'Joseph <b>was</b> shepherding his brothers' — yesterday 'his feet were hurt with fetters'; now 'and Joseph was the ruler.' And 'Moses <b>was</b> shepherding' — yesterday he fled from Pharaoh; now he drowned his master in water. 'A man <b>was</b> in the land of Uz, Job was his name' — yesterday 'he pours out my bile to the earth'; now 'and HaShem restored all that was Job's, doubled.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:27.592163838Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}